title: Cursor IDE Binary Planting via Workspace Git Executable
id: a7c3e1d4-8b2f-4a9e-b6c5-d0f1e2a3b4c5
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects execution of git.exe or hatch.exe from outside standard
    Git installation directories, consistent with the Cursor IDE
    binary-planting vulnerability CVE-2026-63093 (Mindgard, 2026).
    On affected Windows configurations, Cursor resolves Git-related
    executables during workspace initialization and executes a
    malicious binary planted in the repository root before the
    legitimate system binary is found.
references:
    - https://cyberpress.org/cursor-0-day-allows-arbitrary-code-execution/
    - https://gbhackers.com/cursor-0-day-lets-attackers-execute-malicious-code/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/08/19
tags:
    - attack.t1034
    - attack.t1204
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_git:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\git.exe'
    selection_hatch:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\hatch.exe'
    filter_standard_git:
        Image|startswith:
            - 'C:\Program Files\Git'
            - 'C:\Program Files (x86)\Git'
    filter_standard_hatch:
        Image|startswith:
            - 'C:\Users\*\AppData\Local\pipx'
            - 'C:\Users\*\AppData\Roaming\Python'
    condition:
        (selection_git and not filter_standard_git) or
        (selection_hatch and not filter_standard_hatch)
falsepositives:
    - Portable or self-contained Git installations outside Program Files
    - Developer tools that bundle git.exe in non-standard paths
level: high
